  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math>&nbsp;be a differentiable function such that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>. Then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>210</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
